From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:46:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): refuse switches under any admitted turn and
 preserve queued intent [daveey]

Review rework: the active holder must be checked regardless of whether admission preceded the snapshot. Guard unmanaged in-place swaps too. Low-level refusal promises no replay; the gateway queues with original pin_session_override, persist_override and count_switch flags and replays them unchanged. Rebased onto the corrected custody change from PR #3814, preserving route resets.

Proof: removing the managed and unmanaged active-holder guards makes both pre-snapshot regression cases fail (2/2). Event-ordered post-snapshot test exercises the next real provider dispatch with network I/O stubbed. All 129 direct switch/deferred consumers: 2420 passed, 1 skipped. scripts/check --base origin/main: all 21 checks pass.

